    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0291" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72111 Ap 4/60</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 3, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose herewith a
                    proposed note in reply to the memorandum of the German Government on the subject
                    of the <hi rendition="#italic">Appam</hi> which was received by me on March
                        16th.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d207-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I do not believe that it is advisable to arbitrate the question but I naturally
                    dislike to refuse arbitration on account of our previous attitude on the
                    subject. The note is prepared with the idea of avoiding arbitration in this
                    particular case.</p>
                <p>I would be much obliged if you would make any suggestions as to the form of the
                    note.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d207-f1" n="65" xml:id="d207-f1-content">
                <p>For the German memorandum, see <ref target="frus1916Supp#pg_733">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p. 733</ref>; for the reply as sent, see
                        <ref target="frus1916Supp#pg_735">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p. 735</ref>.</p>
            </note>
